<MainLayout title="Women’s Recovery Housing"><PageHero eyebrow="Women’s housing" title="Safety, structure, and a community of recovery." intro="Recovery housing for adult women in Pittsburgh, with the privacy and consistency needed to build a stable next chapter." image="/images/womens-community.jpg" imageAlt="Women talking together in a bright community room" />
<section class="section"><div class="container grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Women’s residences</p><h2>A dependable environment for daily recovery.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Our women’s housing provides a substance-free community where residents can strengthen routines, relationships, and independence.</p><p>New Beginnings serves women in Brighton Heights and the greater Pittsburgh area. For resident privacy, exact locations are never published online.</p><ul class="rule-list"><li><strong>Dignity and privacy</strong>Resident safety guides how we share information and operate our homes.</li><li><strong>Shared recovery</strong>Peer connection helps turn individual effort into a dependable community.</li><li><strong>Practical stability</strong>Daily structure supports continued work toward personal recovery goals.</li></ul></div></div></section><InquiryForm title="Ask about women’s housing" /></MainLayout>
